  "title": "Chapter 40: Minerals and Resources of India",
  "order": 40,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "36g23b2",
      "content": "Minerals are naturally occurring inorganic substances found in the Earth's crust. They have a definite chemical composition and physical properties. Minerals are very important for industrial development, energy production, transportation and infrastructure. India possesses a wide variety of mineral resources due to its diverse geological structure."
    },
