    {
      "id": "dk0yut8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Mineral Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Minerals in India are broadly classified into Metallic (Ferrous and Non-Ferrous) and Non-Metallic (Inorganic and Mineral Fuels).",
        "Major mineral belts include the Chota Nagpur Belt, the North-Western Region, the South-Western Plateau, and the South-Eastern Region.",
        "Coal is India's most important fossil fuel, distributed primarily in Gondwana rock formations and Tertiary deposits.",
        "Petroleum resources are concentrated in onshore and offshore basins including Mumbai High, Assam (Digboi, Naharkatia), and Gujarat (Ankleshwar).",
        "Sustainable development requires careful conservation, recycling, and efficient utilization of non-renewable mineral resources."
      ],
      "id": "866m3pr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f94k3ep",
      "content": "• Minerals are natural substances found in rocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vuutktv",
      "content": "• They are formed through geological processes over millions of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0mti9ii",
      "content": "• Minerals are essential raw materials for industries."
    },
